# Play ViZDoom Health Gathering

The floor damages your health over time. Medkits appear around the rectangular
arena and restore health when collected. Survive as long as possible, ideally
to the natural game timeout. Do not stop after a positive reward or a pickup.
Continue until a state says `done: true`.

Use only the ViZDoom MCP tools. Call `get_current_state` first. It returns the
screen, valid button names, and episode metadata. The controls are `TURN_LEFT`,
`TURN_RIGHT`, and `MOVE_FORWARD`; you can press several together.

Before each `make_action`, write a visible note of at most 60 words:
`Situation:` describe relevant visual facts; `Decision:` give the immediate
goal, chosen buttons, repetition count, and expected result. Pass the same
text as `situation` and `decision` in
`{"buttons": [...], "repeat": 1, "situation": "...", "decision": "..."}`.
Those text fields are optional in the tool schema for compatibility, but you
must always provide both. `repeat` is 1 or 2; each repetition advances four
frames. Make one `make_action` call per tool invocation, then inspect the new
state before choosing again. Do not loop over many tool calls from one image.

Do not use the internet or access the game through files or any route other
than these tools. Built-in web search and fetch are disabled.
